{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Who, etc.</b> And one wonders how this can be, for HaShem created everything and knows how much water is in the sea, as though He measured it." "<b>In the hollow of His hand.</b> Like בשעלי שעורים (in my handful) (Ezekiel 13:19)." "<b>And the heavens.</b> Which He spread like a tent-curtain — He knows their measure, for He created them in His might according to wisdom, as though He measured them in a span, and Scripture speaks in the manner of men." "<b>And comprehended.</b> Like מדד (measured), and the Targum of וימדו בעומר (and they measured with an omer) (Exodus 16:18) is וכלו." "<b>In a measure.</b> Like משורה (in a third), and it is possible that it is from the root שלש (to divide in three); therefore we do not know today what the ancient measures were, and likewise ותשקמו בדמעות שליש (you make them drink tears by the third) (Psalms 80:6)." "<b>And weighed in the balance.</b> This is what is called קריסתון (steelyard), which has a long arm, and it is from the root פלס (to level/measure) in מעגל (a circle) (Proverbs 4:26)." "<b>And the hills in scales.</b> The meaning is that He places a hill in one pan of the scales and another hill in the other pan, and this is by way of parable."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {4 "The comparison to משורה (a measure of one-third) and the root שלש are preserved literally; Ibn Ezra is noting uncertainty about ancient units."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:11.526754071Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}